 "description": "A juvenile Belatz: 2 body regions (B2), a head, 2 eyes, a 2-leaf crest, 2 legs, 2 flaps, a tail; feathers; upright, neck head. Coat: colour cobalt; fluff between; sheen between; feathers between; fur reach body only; second colour butter. Face: head large; beak long; crest low; crown tall; eyes small, close. Shape: waist thin; back line arched; hind body small; body pear; build slim. Legs & tail: tail curl hangs; tail long, thick. Proportions: a large body, a big head, the head carried low, a long beak, small eyes, a tall crest, a low feather crest, long legs, broad feet, a thin waist, an arched back, a long tail, the tail hanging, wide flaps.",
